  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on comparing the variances of the two lotteries and preferring the one with the larger variance. Lottery A yields 500 Euros with 100% probability, so its expected value is 500 and its variance is 0 (since there is no deviation from the mean). Lottery B yields 1000 Euros with 50% probability and 0 Euros with 50% probability, so its expected value is (0.5 × 1000) + (0.5 × 0) = 500, and its variance is (0.5 × (1000 - 500)^2) + (0.5 × (0 - 500)^2) = 0.5 × 250000 + 0.5 × 250000 = 250000. Thus, Lottery B has a higher variance than Lottery A. The decision reason would prefer Lottery B due to its higher variance. The information needed to apply this reason is available in the decision problem.",
